  "notes": "American adult-contemporary pop-rock with a wordy, list-like topline: 78–142 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature ballads at 79–90. Harmony is C major and other open-string majors running I–V–vi–IV \"with a mixolydian ♭VII on the pre-chorus\", and the ballads \"add a string-pad-supported IV–I plagal ending\" — all three are authored families and mixolydian carries real weight in the scales. Three drum deltas are quoted: \"kick 1 and 3\", \"snare 2&4 with a wide reverb\", and \"8th hat opening to a ride in the chorus\" plus \"percussion (shaker/tambourine) doubles the 8ths\", which is the four-lane perc block at 3–6 with the ride and a tom for the \"tom-based fill into each chorus\". The bass is \"roots and fifths, 8th notes, with a walk-up into the chorus\", so the fifth and second are its passing tones and the anticipation runs high. The melody is \"syllable-dense in the verse (near-spoken), then a wide sustained chorus\", which is the 4–11 density over a wide register with an arch contour. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 85, which is the centre of the stated ballad band rather than a published figure.",
